# 18. Design Rationale

### Why Docker?

Docker packages the application and its dependencies into a reproducible deployment artifact.

### Why ECS?

ECS provides service-level management of the container, including task lifecycle and deployment management.

### Why Fargate?

Fargate removes the need to provision and manage EC2 instances. Compute resources are allocated directly to the ECS task.

### Why an ALB?

The ALB provides a stable public endpoint and separates the public interface from individual ECS task IP addresses. It also performs health checks and routes traffic only to healthy targets.

### Why a target group?

The target group provides the connection between the ALB and the ECS tasks and defines how the backend targets are health-checked.

### Why CloudWatch Logs?

CloudWatch provides centralized visibility into application and container behaviour during deployment and operation.

